{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateFSTrichotomy","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.separation_requires_the_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.separation_requires_the_channel","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L170-L177","doc":"The two halves as one statement: object data is never enough, and the channel\nis enough. This is the file's content in a single type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.some_channel_gate_separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.some_channel_gate_separates","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L157-L168","doc":"**The obstruction lifts.** A gate allowed to read the Young-symmetry channel\nin addition to the object data does separate the two — exhibited concretely, so\nthis is a construction and not an existence claim.\n\nRead together with `no_object_gate_separates`: the channel is not merely *a*\nplace a discriminator could live, it is the first place one can live at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourChannel_ne_flavourChannels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourChannel_ne_flavourChannels","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L151-L155","doc":"The colour channel differs from **both** flavour channels, so the distinction\nis not an artefact of which flavour multiplet is chosen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourOctetChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourOctetChannel","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L148-L149","doc":"The octet's flavour channel is the mixed one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourDecupletChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourDecupletChannel","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The decuplet's flavour channel is the symmetric one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourChannel","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L141-L143","doc":"Colour occupies the totally antisymmetric channel: the baryon colour\nwavefunction is `ε_{abc}`. **Input, not derived here** — see the header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instReprChannel3.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instReprChannel3.repr","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instReprChannel3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instReprChannel3","kind":"instance","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqChannel3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqChannel3","kind":"instance","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.antisymmetric","kind":"ctor","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L137-L138","doc":"`λ = (1³)`, the sign irrep: the colour channel, `ε_{abc}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.mixed","kind":"ctor","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L135-L136","doc":"`λ = (2,1)`, the standard irrep: the octet's flavour channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3.symmetric","kind":"ctor","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L133-L134","doc":"`λ = (3)`, the trivial `S₃`-irrep: the decuplet's flavour channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.Channel3","kind":"inductive","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L130-L139","doc":"The Young-symmetry channel of `V ⊗ V ⊗ V`, indexed by the partitions of 3 —\nequivalently by the irreps of `S₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.tensor_cube_gates_also_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.tensor_cube_gates_also_blind","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L113-L128","doc":"**The next moves are already dead.** After `Sym²` fails, the natural\ninstinct is to try the next tensor functor — `Sym³`, or `Λ³` (whose singlet is\nthe colour `ε_{abc}`, which makes it look especially promising). Both dimensions\nare functions of `dim V` alone, so a gate reading either is a gate reading\n`ObjectData`, and `no_object_gate_separates` already covers it.\n\nChecked concretely rather than argued: `Sym³` gives `10` for both triples and\n`Λ³` gives `1` for both.\n\nThis is what makes the class exclusion worth having. It does not merely record\ntwo past failures — it forecloses the entire \"try another tensor construction on\n`V`\" family without running any of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.alt3Dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.alt3Dim","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L110-L111","doc":"Dimension of the alternating cube of a `d`-dimensional space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.sym3Dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.sym3Dim","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L107-L108","doc":"Dimension of the symmetric cube of a `d`-dimensional space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.no_object_invariant_separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.no_object_invariant_separates","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The same, for an invariant valued in an arbitrary type rather than a\ntwo-valued verdict — nothing about the exclusion depends on the gate being a\nyes/no test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.no_object_gate_separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.no_object_gate_separates","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**The class exclusion.** A gate is a verdict-valued function of what it can\nread. No gate that reads only object-level data separates the colour triple from\nthe flavour triple — not the two already tried, and not any third.\n\nThis is why the `Sym²` and `ℤ/3` failures were not repairable: they were not\nfailures of those two constructions, but of the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colour_eq_flavour_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colour_eq_flavour_data","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L85-L88","doc":"The two triples carry **identical** object-level data. The dimensions arrive\nby genuinely different routes — `(7-1)/2` from the octonion decomposition,\n`2·1·3/2` from the Weyl dimension formula — and agree at 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourTripleData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.flavourTripleData","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L77-L83","doc":"The flavour triple, as the `SU(3)` fundamental with Dynkin label `(1,0)`,\ndimension by the Weyl formula `(a+1)(b+1)(a+b+2)/2`.\n\nHere `FSType.complex` **is** derived: triality `1 ≠ 0`, so the fundamental is not\nself-dual (`fundamental_not_selfDual`), hence complex type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourTripleData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.colourTripleData","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L68-L75","doc":"The colour triple, as the `ℂ³` summand of `Im(𝕆) = ℝ ⊕ ℂ³`: its complex\ndimension is what remains of the seven imaginary directions after the stabilised\nreal line is removed, halved.\n\n`FSType.complex` is the Günaydin–Gürsey input (bean `qou-8pl3`, gap (i)) — a\ncitation here, not a derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqObjectData.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqObjectData.decEq","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqObjectData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.instDecidableEqObjectData","kind":"instance","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.tri","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.fs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.fs","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.dim","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.FlavourColourDiscriminator.ObjectData","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/FlavourColourDiscriminator.lean#L58-L66","doc":"The object-level data this chapter's gates actually read: a dimension, a\nFrobenius–Schur type, and a triality class. Both the `Sym²` gate (at dimension\nthree, `gate_forces_complex_of_dim_three` shows its verdict is exactly the\nFrobenius–Schur type) and the `ℤ/3` selection rule factor through this. ","signatureChunk":0}]}